# ATLAS analysis on Unity

This project runs on a Slurm compute node inside an EL9 Apptainer container.
Before starting Codex, the user selects the ATLAS release with asetup and
sources any local build setup. Preserve that environment for analysis commands.

- Read PROJECT_CONTEXT.md for the exact release, build setup, input paths,
  resource limits, and the current task. Ask if a required value is missing.
- At the start of a new session, check the hostname, /etc/os-release, working
  directory, Python executable, ATLAS release, and import ROOT. Check only the
  necessary environment variables; do not dump the entire environment.
- Run analysis with the release's Python and libraries. Do not activate the
  MCP Pixi environment in the analysis shell or install packages into CVMFS.
- Use atlas-rucio for dataset/replica discovery and atlas-ami for metadata and
  provenance. Bound queries and report exact dataset names and scopes.
- Start with discovery only. Do not create/delete replication rules, change
  catalogs, download large datasets, or submit large jobs without the user's
  explicit request specifying the intended operation and resources.
- The user creates and renews their VOMS proxy outside the agent conversation.
  Never print or copy private keys, proxy contents, passphrases, auth.json, or
  access tokens into messages, logs, source files, or commits. If credentials
  expire, tell the user to renew them and restart the MCP processes.
- Run builds and tests within the allocated CPU, memory, time, and GPU limits.
  Do not request another allocation from inside this one.
- Explain changes, run a small relevant test, and keep large production runs
  separate from validation.
